t":"எருது","lemma":"erutu","gloss":"ox"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"as"}],"gloss":"as oxen"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வாள்தக","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"vāḷ","gloss":"sword"},{"text":"தக","lemma":"taka","gloss":"fittingly"}],"gloss":"fittingly with swords"},{"surface":"வைகலும்","parts":[{"text":"வைகல்","lemma":"vaikal","gloss":"day"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"every"}],"gloss":"every day"},{"surface":"உழக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"உழக்கு","lemma":"uḻakku","gloss":"thresh/churn"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"will"}],"gloss":"threshing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மாட்சி","parts":[{"text":"மாட்சி","lemma":"māṭci","gloss":"greatness/glory"}],"gloss":"greatness"},{"surface":"யவர்","parts":[{"text":"யவர்","lemma":"யவர்","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"they","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இவள்","parts":[{"text":"இவள்","lemma":"ivaḷ","gloss":"this girl's"}],"gloss":"this girl's"},{"surface":"தன்னை","parts":[{"text":"தன்னை","lemma":"taṉṉai","gloss":"brothers"}],"gloss":"brothers"},{"surface":"மாரே","parts":[{"text":"மார்","lemma":"mār","gloss":"plural suffix"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Forest crow's dark wing resembling / mayilai-garlanded, great-shouldered young girl / 'Of what class is she, this girl?' thus with trembling excitement / with me asks, victorious-speared great lord! / Lakshmi-desirable fitting quality's her beauty / to warriors except, to others will not become. / Green-legged heron's wide-open-mouthed chick / soft mud close-by bank having foraged and eaten, after that, / āral fish laid mustard-like eggs / sharp fine prawn's chick-with obtains / his wet-field lord, her father. And kings / because of not obtaining, great battle because of waging, / abundant corpses piled-high stacks, wounded elephants as oxen, / with swords fittingly every day threshing / greatness-possessing they, this girl's brothers indeed!","translation":"The great lord with a victorious spear asks me in trembling excitement, 'Who is this young girl with beautiful shoulders and a garland of mayilai flowers, whose hair resembles the dark wings of a forest crow?' Her beauty, worthy of Lakshmi's desire, belongs only to fierce warriors and to no one else. Her father is the lord of fertile wet fields where the wide-mouthed chick of a green-legged heron, after foraging on the soft muddy bank, finds the mustard-like eggs laid by the āral fish along with the young of sharp-nosed prawns. Because the kings could not obtain her, they wage a great battle. In that field, her glorious brothers use swords to thresh daily, treating the high piles of corpses as stacks of grain and the fallen elephants as the threshing oxen!","modern":"காட்டுக் காகத்தின் கரிய சிறகைப் போன்ற கூந்தலையும், மயிலைப் பூ மாலையையும், பெரிய தோள்களையும் உடைய இந்த இளம்பெண், 'எந்தக் குலத்தைச் சேர்ந்தவள்?' என்று என்னிடம் நடுக்கத்துடனும் ஆசையுடனும் கேட்கிறான் வெற்றிவேல் ஏந்திய தலைவன். திருமகள் விரும்பத்தக்க அழகுடைய இவளது நலம், வீரர்களுக்கு மட்டுமே உரியது; மற்றவர்களுக்குக் கிடைக்காது. பசுமையான கால்களையுடைய கொக்கின் அகன்ற வாயையுடைய குஞ்சு, மென்மையான சேற்றையுடைய கரையில் மேய்ந்து உண்ட பிறகு, ஆரல் மீன் ஈன்ற கடுகு போன்ற முட்டைகளையும், கூர்மையான இறால் மீனின் குஞ்சுகளையும் எளிதாகப் பெறுகின்ற வளமான வயல்களுக்குத் தலைவன் இவளது தந்தை. இவளைப் பெண் கேட்டுப் பெறாததால் வேந்தர்கள் போர் தொடுக்கின்றனர். அந்தப் போர்க்களத்தில், குவிந்து கிடக்கும் பிணங்களை நெற்போராகவும், வீழ்ந்த யானைகளை எருதுகளாகவும் கொண்டு, வாள்களைக் கொண்டு நாள்தோறும் போர் உழவு செய்யும் பெருமை மிக்கவர்கள் இவளுடைய சகோதரர்கள்!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Makaṭpāṟ Kāñci theme within the Kāñci tiṇai, which depicts the refusal of a daughter's hand in marriage to powerful kings, resulting in a fierce battle. The speaker addresses a great lord who has fallen in love with the girl and is anxiously asking about her lineage. The speaker warns him that her beauty is meant only for true warriors, as her family is fiercely proud and powerful. Her father is a wealthy lord of the fertile agricultural region, described through the imagery of a heron chick easily finding abundant food in the rich fields. Because the kings were refused, a terrible war is fought where her brothers show their martial prowess. The poet uses a striking agricultural metaphor for the battlefield, where the brothers 'thresh' daily using swords, treating heaps of corpses as grain-stacks and wounded elephants as threshing oxen.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.3],[0.3,0.7],[1.15,1.6],[1.67,2.1],[2.1,2.75],[2.75,3.4],[3.4,3.9],[3.9,4.73],[4.73,5.23],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,6.1],[6.1,6.3],[6.3,6.9],[6.9,7.35],[7.35,7.8],[7.8,8.2],[8.2,8.7],[8.96,9.22],[9.22,9.49],[9.49,10.8],[10.8,11.0],[11.0,11.3],[11.3,12.3],[12.3,12.9],[12.9,13.3],[13.47,13.8],[13.8,14.8],[14.8,15.1],[15.1,15.3],[15.3,15.7],[15.93,16.87],[17.1,17.44],[17.44,18.12],[18.12,18.5],[19.12,19.42],[19.42,19.72],[19.72,20.12],[20.12,20.52],[20.52,21.42],[21.42,21.92],[21.92,22.25],[22.42,22.77],[22.77,23.37],[23.37,24.22],[24.22,24.82],[24.82,25.32],[25.32,25.84],[25.84,26.62],[26.62,27.12],[27.12,27.98],[27.98,28.83],[28.83,29.18],[29.18,29.52],[29.52,29.75],[29.75,30.09],[30.21,30.82],[30.82,31.42],[31.42,31.62],[31.62,32.92],[32.92,33.12],[33.12,33.38],[33.38,33.65],[33.65,33.82]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.6],[1.68,2.2],[2.2,3.36],[3.36,3.6],[3.6,4.1],[4.1,5.06],[5.06,5.63],[5.7,6.0],[6.0,6.8],[6.8,7.0],[7.0,7.3],[7.3,7.95],[7.95,8.6],[8.6,9.4],[9.4,10.18],[10.18,10.95],[10.95,11.1],[11.1,11.9],[11.9,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,13.8],[13.8,14.4],[14.4,14.9],[14.9,15.4],[15.4,16.5],[16.5,16.9],[16.9,17.1],[17.1,17.6],[17.6,17.9],[17.9,18.2],[18.2,18.5],[18.5,18.8],[21.44,21.74],[21.74,22.04],[22.04,22.54],[22.54,22.94],[22.94,24.04],[24.04,24.54],[24.54,25.04],[25.04,25.48],[25.48,26.23],[26.23,27.29],[27.29,28.04],[28.04,28.54],[28.54,29.06],[29.06,29.43],[29.43,29.92],[29.92,30.54],[30.54,30.73],[30.73,31.1],[31.1,31.84],[31.84,33.27],[33.27,33.74],[33.74,34.3],[34.64,35.04],[35.04,35.78],[35